infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title The seven production index failure modes — each with its one-line diagnostic
  desc Every production index postmortem maps to one of these seven; the diagnosis is always EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) on the exact query
  lists
    - label Missing index on FK column
      desc Postgres indexes the referenced PK, never the referencing column. ON DELETE CASCADE does an O(n) Seq Scan of the child table — a DELETE that takes 7 minutes holding row locks. Fix — CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY on every FK column.
    - label Implicit type coercion defeats the index
      desc WHERE bigint_col = '42' (TEXT vs BIGINT) casts the column on every row, so the planner cannot walk the B-tree and falls to Seq Scan. Fix — typed parameters ($1::BIGINT), and range predicates instead of created_at::date.
    - label Stale statistics cause the wrong plan
      desc Autovacuum only ANALYZEs after 20% of rows change; until then EXPLAIN shows rows=50 when actual is 500,000 — a 10,000x miss that picks a catastrophic nested loop. Fix — ANALYZE after bulk ops, CREATE STATISTICS for skewed multi-column data.
    - label Index bloat slows scans
      desc Dead entries from updates and deletes grow the index to 5-10x its expected size; queries stay slow despite using it. Fix — REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY on indexes past 30% bloat (pgstattuple_approx), scheduled off-peak.
    - label Wrong composite column order
      desc A composite (status, workspace_id) does not accelerate queries filtering by workspace_id alone — a leading-column violation that falls back to Seq Scan. Fix — add a second index with the correct leading column or redesign the composite.
    - label JSONB GIN cardinality bomb
      desc A GIN index over a JSONB column with millions of unique keys grows 10-50x the column size, evicts hot heap pages from shared_buffers, and spikes insert latency. Fix — expression B-tree indexes on known-hot fields like (payload->>'event_type').
    - label Has an index but still slow
      desc The right index exists but the structure is wrong — ORDER BY column not in the index forces a full sort, no INCLUDE means heap fetches dominate, or the leading column misses the most selective filter. Fix — EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS), then a covering composite that serves filter and sort.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #14b8a6
